{%- comment -%}
  The catalogue card, in the vocabulary the designed site draws it in:
  .piece / .piece__media / .piece__info, with the badge, wishlist heart,
  quick-add label, name, craft line, price (+ struck-through was) and the
  colour swatches.

  Every value is the real product's. The craft line is the `shrujan.craft`
  metafield, drawn only where a product has one; the swatch discs are the
  `shrujan.swatches` colour list; the badge is decided by snippets/piece-badge,
  which reads the two prices before it reads a metafield.

  Accepts: product (required), show_swatches, quick_label, sold_out_label,
  sale_badge (false to suppress the computed "N% off").
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  comment
    The craft line is the craft and nothing else. It used to fall back to the
    product type, which on a real catalogue is "clothing" on some pieces and
    blank on others: a row of cards with the line on half of them, each price
    a line lower than its neighbour's.
  endcomment
  assign card_craft = product.metafields.shrujan.craft.value

  comment
    Normalised to a real boolean before it travels on: an omitted `sale_badge`
    means the computed badge stays on, which is the packaged behaviour.
  endcomment
  assign card_sale_on = true
  if sale_badge == false
    assign card_sale_on = false
  endif

  assign card_swatch_list = product.metafields.shrujan.swatches.value

  assign card_was = false
  if product.compare_at_price > product.price
    assign card_was = true
  endif
-%}
<a class="piece" href="{{ product.url }}">
  <div class="piece__media">
    {%- if product.featured_image -%}
      <img src="{{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 900 }}" alt="{{ product.featured_image.alt | default: product.title | escape }}" loading="lazy">
    {%- else -%}
      {{ 'product-1' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'piece__ph' }}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- render 'piece-badge', product: product, sale: card_sale_on, sold_out_label: sold_out_label -%}
    <button class="piece__wish" type="button" aria-label="Save {{ product.title | escape }} to wishlist"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 19.8S4.5 15.3 4.5 9.9c0-2.6 2-4.4 4.2-4.4 1.5 0 2.7.8 3.3 2 .6-1.2 1.8-2 3.3-2 2.2 0 4.2 1.8 4.2 4.4 0 5.4-7.5 9.9-7.5 9.9Z"></path></svg></button>
    {%- comment -%}
      The label the design already carries, made to work: the variant travels on
      the element and the rail's own script posts it to the cart. A piece that
      cannot be bought keeps the label and simply opens, as it did before.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <span class="piece__quick"{% if product.available %} data-variant="{{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant.id }}"{% endif %}>{{ quick_label | default: 'Add to bag' }}</span>
  </div>
  <div class="piece__info">
    <p class="piece__name">{{ product.title }}</p>
    {%- if card_craft != blank -%}
      <p class="piece__craft">{{ card_craft }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
    <p class="piece__price">{{ product.price | money | strip_html }}{% if card_was %}<span>{{ product.compare_at_price | money | strip_html }}</span>{% endif %}</p>
    {%- if show_swatches and card_swatch_list.size > 0 -%}
      <span class="piece__swatches" aria-hidden="true">{% for card_swatch in card_swatch_list limit: 5 %}<i style="background: {{ card_swatch }}"></i>{% endfor %}</span>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</a>
